  (text "RP2350A, as Raspberry Pi's minimal design: Hardware design with RP2350"
    (at 91.44 15.24 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "1884d07f-3822-4f01-bbec-05c1d113606e")
  )
  (text "VDD is the RP2350's own 3.3 V, up whenever 5 V is. +3V3 is the Pi's."
    (at 91.44 21.59 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "8a2058b5-a201-4c20-88e1-5603e09fd7a4")
  )
  (text "Core regulator: L1 has a polarity mark. Lay it out as the Pico 2 does."
    (at 213.36 45.72 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "5aacdce2-0e28-483a-b8a1-44d17d7cb20d")
  )
  (text "To the Pi through 1 k and 330 R. While the Pi's 3.3 V is down (GPIO14 low),"
    (at 274.32 78.74 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "1d487a41-dbe9-4b21-b8df-1fec99b81582")
  )
  (text "the firmware keeps MCU_TX an input, so a Pi in standby is not back-powered."
    (at 274.32 84.328 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "a9f68433-5176-4ce4-99f3-35fdd14fb362")
  )
  (text "The Pi resets the RP2350 by driving PI_RUN high"
    (at 101.6 85.09 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "0488d9da-831b-4eed-9e9d-6ef46a23afb0")
  )
  (text "Is the Pi's 3.3 V up?"
    (at 284.48 120.65 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "cbc349b6-35ba-4476-a78a-8046f675b12d")
  )
